  <layout>One page of text: a Latin poem in verse, set as 7 stanzas of four lines each, indented in a staggered pattern. Catchword at the lower right, below the last line. No margin notes.</layout>
  <page_number>36</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIACA,</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Hinc</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Hic dum sagaces prouidus explicat</l>
    <l n="2">Curas,amicis dum timet anxius</l>
    <l n="3">Hostisque dum fraudes recludit,</l>
    <l n="4">Quæ mala,quoue tulit labores !</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Nullæ rigenti frigore territum</l>
    <l n="6">Videre Brumæ aut Andromedes Pater,</l>
    <l n="7">Et stella vesani Leonis,</l>
    <l n="8">Cum segetes coquit æstus almas.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">Tantisque tandem mortibus addite,</l>
    <l n="10">Condæ Princeps,quo tua carmine</l>
    <l n="11">Dicenda,quo sletu riganda</l>
    <l n="12">Fata truci properata fraude?</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">Non præliantem perdidit hostilicus</l>
    <l n="14">Ensis duello,classica cum sonant,</l>
    <l n="15">Armata quando militantes</l>
    <l n="16">Per medias rapit ira cædes.</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">Sed tu occidisti,progenies bona</l>
    <l n="18">Magni parentis,Borbonicæ altera</l>
    <l n="19">Spes gentis occultis venen-</l>
    <l n="20">is Insidiis superatus atri,</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">Quo delibutis muneribus ferox</l>
    <l n="22">Medea quondam Colchica pellicem</l>
    <l n="23">Est vlta,quo parens superbis</l>
    <l n="24">Sæviit imperiis Locusta.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">Has prisca fraudes Gallia nesciens</l>
    <l n="26">Virtute sola &amp; Marte potentior</l>
    <l n="27">Latè per obstantes caternas</l>
    <l n="28">Explicuit sua signa victrix</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Two ornamental signs before "Andromedes" (line 6) and "Marte" (line 26) appear to be astronomical or planetary symbols; I could not read them with certainty, so I did not transcribe them. The stanza breaks follow the indentation pattern; the verse reads as continuous. Spelling u/v is normalised (e.g. "prouidus" to "providus" in print, but kept as "Vlta" with capital U as printed: "Est vlta" transcribed as "Est vlta"). Show-through from the facing page is ignored.</notes>
</page>
